{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/focusmode_description

    The activity description, without the box core draws around it.

    Focus mode replaces the activity information render - core's whole core_course/activity_info
    template - with this one. That render is the only place the activity description appears,
    since Moodle 4.0 moved the intro out of every module's own page and into the activity header,
    so blanking it would take away a forum's or a page's intro text, not chrome. This template
    keeps the description and leaves the box, the region marker and the completion half out.

    The wrapper reproduces what core writes around the same value - the activity-description
    class and the intro id, from course/templates/activity_info.mustache - so a module's own
    stylesheet, and anything anchoring at the intro id, keeps working. The has-automatic-completion
    modifier core adds there is deliberately not reproduced: it exists to close the gap to the
    completion box below the description, and in focus mode there is no box under it.

    The value is triple-stashed because it is finished HTML: activity_header builds it with
    format_module_intro(), which has already run the text through format_text().

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a Mustache
    comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * description - the activity intro, already rendered by format_module_intro(), trusted HTML

    Example context (json):
    {
        "description": "<div class=\"no-overflow\"><p>Read the protocol before the session.</p></div>"
    }
}}
<div class="activity-description dimensions-focus-description" id="intro">
    {{{ description }}}
</div>
